/* book: lead: A buck converter steps a DC voltage down. A switch chops the input. An inductor and capacitor average the pulses, so the output is smooth and lower than the input. The diode gives inductor current a path when the switch opens. Gain comes from the duty ratio D, not a lossy resistor. Buck converters sit inside phones and laptops (battery chargers and processor supplies), LED drivers and car USB char */
