/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The buck converter has source Vs, switch S, freewheeling diode Df, inductor L, capacitor C and load resistor R.
   - When S is ON for Ton, the input connects to L and the diode is reverse biased.
   - L in henries, iL in amperes, t in seconds.
   - The inductor integrates this voltage.
   - Apply volt-second balance.
   - (Vs − Vo)·D·T − Vo·(1−D)·T = 0
   - Divide by T: D(Vs − Vo) = (1−D)Vo, so Vo = D Vs.
   - A real diode has forward drop VD.
   - At light load the inductor current can reach zero before the period ends.
   - During ON, diL/dt = (Vs − Vo)/L.
*/
