/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Draw the boost cell.
   - State ON, switch closed.
   - State OFF, switch open.
   - Let T be the switching period in seconds and D = Ton/T the duty ratio, where Ton is the on-time and Toff = T − Ton is the off-time.
   - Vo is output voltage in V; Vs is source voltage in V; D is duty ratio, between 0 and 1.
   - The gain is at least one and, in theory, grows without limit as D approaches one.
   - During ON, iL rises by ΔIL = Vs·D·T/L.
   - ΔIL = Vs·D/(fs·L)
   - ΔIL is peak-to-peak inductor ripple current in A; fs = 1/T is switching frequency in Hz; L is inductance in H.
   - IL is average inductor current in A; Io = Vo/R is load current in A; R is load resistance in Ω.
*/
