/* book exam traps: Writing Vo = Vs·D or Vo = Vs/(1 + D). The boost gain is Vs/(1 − D), so D = 1 − Vs/Vo. | Forgetting the (1 − D) in the current transfer. The average inductor current is IL = Io/(1 − D), and the switch carries IL, not Io. | Saying the diode conducts during the on-time. It is reverse biased then; it conducts only during the off-time. | Using the buck ripple formula. In a boost the inductor sees Vs during the on-time, so ΔIL = Vs·D·T/L. | Ignoring the output capacitor duty. C alone feeds the load during the on-time, giving ΔVo = Io·D/(fs·C); ESR makes the measured ripple larger. */
